course: dictionary
lesson: 13998
title: Words that show care
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone does something. Lovingly is one of them. It tells you the way a person acts: with love and care. «Mum looked lovingly at her sleeping baby.» Mum's look is full of love, so lovingly means with love.
explain: Lovingly can also mean very carefully and gently, with great attention. «Grandad lovingly fixed the old clock, one tiny wheel at a time.» Grandad is not rushing. He takes great care because he wants the clock to work well. The word about how he did it, and the careful actions around it, are your clues.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. «Mum looked with love at her sleeping baby» still makes sense, so you have it right. Look for the feeling or the care behind the action.
fact: Lovingly is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Lovingly» means in a way that shows love and care.
fact: «Lovingly» can also mean very carefully and gently, with great attention.
fact: Phrases you may see: look lovingly at, lovingly made, lovingly restored, lovingly cared for.
fact: «Lovingly restored» means carefully repaired, with great attention to every detail.
exercise: «Mum looked lovingly at her sleeping baby.» What does lovingly show? | Anger at the noise | *Love and care | Boredom | Surprise at a loud sound
exercise: «Grandad lovingly fixed the old clock, one tiny wheel at a time.» What does lovingly suggest about how he worked? | He gave up on the job | He was angry with the clock | He was careless and in a hurry | *He was very careful and gentle, paying close attention
exercise: «The quilt was lovingly made by my great-gran.» What does lovingly mean here? | Made of plastic | In a hurry, to finish fast | Only half finished | *With great care and love
test: «The nurse lovingly cared for the lost puppy.» How did the nurse care for the puppy? | *Gently and with great kindness | Roughly and quickly | Ignoring it completely | Far away from it
test: Which phrase means that someone repaired something with great care? | loudly shouted | barely noticed | *lovingly restored | quickly thrown away
exam: Ella says, «Dad lovingly packed my lunch every day.» What does this tell us? | *Dad packed it with love and care | Dad packed it in a rush and forgot it | Ella packed the lunch herself | Dad did not pack anything at all
